CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.assertion.1\] .* y havocked through a parameter: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[main\.assigns\.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
^\[main\.loop_assigns\.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
--
`__CPROVER_havoc_slice` is implemented with `__CPROVER_array_replace`, which
the loop assigns inference does not see after inlining the function's body.
The summary that replaces the body of `__VERIFIER_havoc` for the inference
writes the whole object its parameter points to, so the loop havocs y and the
assertion fails. This test fails if the inference inlines the body instead.
